{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"DPoP proof verification — CONTRACT.md §21.7.2 (RFC 9449), contract 1.16."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request"],"title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/iatLeeway"],"title":"Type Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/accessTokenHash(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/canonicalHtu(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/thumbprintS256(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)"],"title":"Type Methods"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The resource-server half of DPoP: given the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DPoP"},{"text":" header a caller presented, decide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether it proves possession for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" request and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" access token, and return","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the key thumbprint that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator\/verifyTokenBinding(_:proofs:)"},{"text":" then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matches against the token’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cnf.jkt"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Why-this-lives-in-the-SDK","type":"heading","text":"Why this lives in the SDK","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"§21.7.2 is a ten-check list, and the contract is blunt about partial implementations:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"“Partial verification is worse than none, because it produces a guard that reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"success.”","type":"text"}]},{"text":" Nine of the ten look optional until someone builds an attack out of the one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that was skipped, so they belong in one audited place rather than in every application","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"guarding an endpoint.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The two most often missing: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"typ"},{"text":" — without pinning it to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dpop+jwt"},{"text":", any ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"other","type":"text"}]},{"text":" JWT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signed by the same key (an access token, an ID token) is replayable as a proof; and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ath"},{"text":" — without it, a proof captured on one request can be re-aimed at a different token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held by the same key.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-algorithm-comes-from-the-key-never-from-the-header","type":"heading","text":"The algorithm comes from the key, never from the header","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"alg: none","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and RSA-public-key-as-HMAC-secret are the same bug wearing different clothes:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"the token told the verifier how to check the token","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":". This enum dispatches on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"embedded key’s own "},{"code":"kty","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"crv","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so an HMAC path is never reachable no matter what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header says."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier"]}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO","symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DpopVerifier","roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DpopVerifier/thumbprintS256(_:)":{"title":"thumbprintS256(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"thumbprintS256"},{"kind":"text","text":"(["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"Any"},{"kind":"text","text":"]) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Compute the RFC 7638 SHA-256 thumbprint of a JWK — the ","type":"text"},{"code":"jkt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/thumbprintS256(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier\/thumbprints256(_:)","type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/document